## Solution notes

- **One query per execution**: `TA_Contact_Queries` is the singleton holder. Its inner `Service` action (Order 1) collects the `AccountId`s from `Trigger.new`, runs a single `Account` query, and **replaces** `accountsById` on every trigger execution (never caches across executions, because later DML in the same transaction can introduce other accounts). The two business actions only read `TA_Contact_Queries.getInstance().accountsById` — they never query.
- **Class name for the metadata record**: the framework resolves the action with `Type.forName(...)`, so the inner class is registered as `TA_Contact_Queries.Service`.
- **Security**: all classes are `inherited sharing` (same as the framework's `MetadataTriggerHandler`), so the query respects the sharing context of the trigger entry point rather than silently escalating it. Records are modified only on `Trigger.new`, never re-queried.
- **Bulk safety**: single SOQL call, single `Map` lookup per record, no DML, no per-record queries — fine for 200+ contacts.
- **Custom metadata**: the metadata relationship field (`Before_Insert__c`) is populated with the DeveloperName of the `sObject_Trigger_Setting__mdt` record (`Contact`); `Description__c` is set on all three records as the package requires.

